WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.830
Lemon juice has a pH of about 2.

2
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.250
Black coffee has a pH of about 5.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.650
Lemon juice has the lower pH,
so it holds more hydrogen ions.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.330
But how many more?

5
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.670
How many times more H⁺ is in the
lemon juice than in the coffee?

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.890
In this mission, you'll find
out what pH really measures,

7
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.690
and calculate pH values
that aren't whole numbers.

8
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:29.300
You'll measure pH two ways, and see how
water itself ionizes, just a little.

9
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:30.610
Your mission:

10
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.320
work out how many times more H⁺ ions
are in lemon juice than in coffee.
